.SH "نام (NAME)"
s1ms2dlf \- convert SunONE Messaging Server SMTP log files to the email DLF
.SH "خلاصه دستور (SYNOPSIS)"
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
\&\fBnms2dlf\fR
.SH "توضیحات (DESCRIPTION)"
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
This program converts a SunONE Messaging Server log file generated by the SMTP
service to the Lire email DLF.  The log file is expected on stdin, the DLF file
is printed to stdout.
.PP
In order to correctly process the log file, you need to turn on logging of the
following channels:
.PP
.Vb 1
\& FIXME
.Ve
.SH LIMITATIONS
.IX Header "LIMITATIONS"
This DLF converter was developed for the SunONE Messaging Server
version 5.2. Other versions may or may not work. Contact the LogReport
developers if you have problems with that converter.
.PP
You can find information about the log format used by SunONE
Messaging Server at the following URL:
.PP
.Vb 1
\&    http://docs.sun.com/source/816\-6009\-10/logging.htm
.Ve
.SS "CONFIGURING LOGGING OF MAILBOX\-DELIVER MODULE"
.IX Subsection "CONFIGURING LOGGING OF MAILBOX-DELIVER MODULE"
We found that there are no logs from the Mailbox\-Delivery module by
default. In order to fix that problem please make sure you do the
following:
.IP 1. 4
Go on the SunONE Messaging Server MTA or Message Store
.IP 2. 4
Become the Mail Server user (usually this should not be root but
typically a user like mailsrv or whatever was defined at installation
time, check for the ownership of the files in your message server
instance for example)
.IP 3. 4
Go to the right location, something like: \fIserver\-root\fR/msg\-instance
.Sp
For example it could be: \fI/opt/sunone/s1ms5/msg\-mymailserver\fR
.IP 4. 4
Do:
.Sp
.Vb 1
\& TO BE WRITTEN
.Ve
.SH "مثال‌ها (EXAMPLES)"
.IX Header "EXAMPLES"
To process a log as produced by Netscape Messaging Server
.PP
.Vb 1
\& $ s1ms2dlf < mail.log
.Ve
.PP
s1ms2dlf will be rarely used on its own, but is more likely
called by lr_log2report:
.PP
.Vb 1
\& $ lr_log2report nms < /var/log/mail.log
.Ve
